{
  "assessment": "The source packet provides a complete experimental and theoretical description of the unitary almost-Mathieu operator (UAMO) and its non-Hermitian extension (PUAMO) realized via single-photon quantum walks. The selected quantitative cluster focuses on the Lyapunov exponent L of the dual PUAMO as a function of the coupling constants lambda_1 and lambda_2, for two fixed values of the non-Hermitian parameter eta: eta=0 (Hermitian regime) and eta=0.1 (non-Hermitian regime). The source reports explicit definitions of lambda_0, the Lyapunov exponent formulas, and the experimental phase diagram measured via the second moment at t=6 for eta=0.1. The extraction captures the central quantitative relations: L = max(0, log(lambda_0)) for eta=0 and L = max(0, log(lambda_0) - 2*pi*eta) for eta=0.1, with lambda_0 = lambda_2*(1+sqrt(1-lambda_1^2))/(lambda_1*(1+sqrt(1-lambda_2^2))). The source provides sufficient numeric controls, readouts, and quantitative mechanisms to support an objective source-grounded response, so case_authoring_ready is set to true.",
